[17592186435411 1078 #edb/ref 17592186435405 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435411 1079 #uuid "ff7fbe60-b6cb-5ed1-81ce-867918d895ff" 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435412 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435409 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435412 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435411 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435412 1069 "q-278319" 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435412 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435412 1071 "The center of the ellipse $\\frac{(x+3)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-5)^{2}}{25}=1$ is located at the point$\\,($\n{{field-1}},\n{{field-2}}$).$" 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435412 1072 #uuid "257a594e-f07f-5439-bc42-9479c53748a8" 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435412 1074 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $h=-3$ and $k=5,$ so the center is located at $(-3,5\\,).$" 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435413 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435410 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435413 1069 "q-16551" 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435413 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435413 1071 "![](images/0f/0faaa905476ef6b6224a4b6b24ceb1adde4b14680507a7c6289885dce1bdd997.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435413 1072 #uuid "37e33b7e-4ee9-510a-871b-336b8d3b6afc" 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435413 1074 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(3,-1),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=3,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=5.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{25} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435414 1068 #edb/ref 17592186435408 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435414 1069 "q-70482" 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435414 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435414 1071 "![](images/a9/a9278747563bf79a79e5633f2fae6d97a6ba021c38e8238ef9d22d1396df0be6.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435414 1072 #uuid "8116a58f-3c71-50dd-834a-34d7c8e130b8" 13194139534765 17592186045417 true] [17592186435414 1074 "Remember that the general equation of an ellipse centered at $(h,k)$ with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the ellipse is centered at $(-2,-2),$ the horizontal radius has length $a=4,$ and the vertical radius has length $b=2.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-(-2))^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-2))^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534765 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-1a520ba4-1bc5-52a1-8b92-4fc8f8534ee4" 17592186435396 "answer-442cd84d-41ff-5be9-a617-0975ae88405b" 17592186435397 "answer-67c9df9f-085a-5a77-b0da-da891883eb22" 17592186435398 "answer-697185c8-8a32-538c-a5da-d37c0206b23f" 17592186435399 "answer-940a5b9f-f125-53e4-989b-e5108b954ad8" 17592186435400 "answer-9d0bb612-0c9d-520f-8d2d-1cd458c72942" 17592186435401 "answer-bb8a8e9f-72f4-5ce4-95d3-47d